# Raw Hyper3D Rodin output (art/raw/*.glb) - ~24 MB of INTERMEDIATES. The
# rigged, game-ready results are committed under assets/chars/, which is the
# artifact that matters. These are excluded rather than kept because they are
# reproducible for free: art/generate_chars.py holds every prompt verbatim and
# generation costs nothing (only DOWNLOAD spends credits), so `python
# art/generate_chars.py` rebuilds them. The previews and the manifest ARE kept -
# they are a few KB and they document what was generated and from which job.
art/raw/*.glb
art/raw/_build_log.txt
